 "text": "If your goal is planned for 9pm it's up against your whole day, and the day wins. Why do we stop doing things we know are good for us? Reason 14. Every hour adds something, an email, a favor being tired. By evening your goal is last in line and it's the easiest thing to drop. So move it, the first 10 minutes after you wake up, before you touch your phone. Learning Spanish, 10 minutes saying the sentences you actually use. Writing a book, 100 words before you open a single message. 10 minutes at 7 beats an hour planned for 9 because 7 actually happens. Send this to a friend who's starting tonight. That's what Demure is for. Archive your dream today and break it into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one reason a day. Next, why deciding every day quietly ends good habits. What's the goal you keep saving for tonight? The link's in the bio.",
